AI SHOULD NOT PRIMARILY REPLACE COGNITION
SOURCE: 𝙼𝚒𝚔𝚎 🜎 @OhWellMike
It should increase the quality, range, and corrigibility of cognition

USE AI TO IMPROVE THE QUALITY OF YOUR THINKING
NOT MERELY THE QUANTITY OF YOUR OUTPUT

NOT AN ORACLE
A SPARRING PARTNER, SIMULATOR, MEMORY SYSTEM, AND QUESTION GENERATOR

CYCLE
THINK → TEST → REFLECT → REVISE → VERIFY → ACT → OBSERVE → UPDATE

ORACLE MODEL
"Tell me what is true."

COGNITIVE-PARTNER MODEL
"Help me determine what I might be missing."

HUMAN COGNITION NODE
Values • Verification • Responsibility
recursive exchange

AI COGNITION NODE / AI COGNITIVE PARTNER
Challenge • Simulation • Memory • Translation • Generation

FUNDAMENTALS
1. ADVERSARIAL COLLABORATOR
   Attack plans. Steelman opposition. Seek disconfirming evidence.

2. PRE-MORTEM ENGINE
   Failure modes. Second-order effects. Edge cases.

3. SPEC COMPILER
   Intent → goals → context → constraints → criteria → plan

4. SOCRATIC TUTOR
   Questions → counterexamples → explanation → mastery

5. COGNITIVE PROSTHESIS
   Working memory. Decision journal. Knowledge graph. Recall.

6. SIMULATOR
   Scenarios. Negotiations. Multi-agent models. What-if analysis.

7. CROSS-DOMAIN TRANSLATOR
   Map concepts between disciplines. Generate and test analogies.

8. UNCERTAINTY MAPPER
   Known / Unknown / Assumed / Contested + methods for resolution

9. BIAS DETECTOR
   Anchoring. Motivated reasoning. Availability. Base-rate neglect.

10. EXPERIMENT DESIGNER
    Hypothesis → cheap test → evidence → update

11. COMPLEXITY INTERFACE
    Summarize. Cluster. Visualize. Navigate. Preserve provenance.

12. ETHICAL STRESS-TESTER
    Edge cases. Stakeholders. Externalities. Unintended harms.

ADDITIONAL MODULES
CREATIVITY CONSTRAINT ENGINE
Generate → constrain → recombine

META-OPTIMIZER
Improve prompts → workflows → learning loops → decision processes

MIRROR FOR JUDGMENT
Make reasoning visible, corrigible, and revisable

